  "H1 decomposition: the 'no universal winner' clause PASSED (max oracle share 0.58 < 0.90) but the balance-gradient clause FAILED flat (Fermat winner share 1.7% in BOTH extreme balance quintiles; every method's winner share is balance-flat). At this sampler the crossover is organized by p-1/q-1 powersmoothness (N-invisible), not by balance: the script verdict PORTFOLIO-RHO-UNIVERSAL+H3-FAIL encodes the pre-stated clause bundle, but rho is a 58% PLURALITY, not universal.",
  "sampler-dependence scope note: the tasking brief fixed only '600 semiprimes bitlen 32-40'; the within-bitlen factor-size spread (independent wide ranges) dilutes near-square N, which is why the position/Fermat channel is marginal here (2.8% winner share) unlike balanced-bet samplers (cf. position 5.19x law).",
